Why is locale-aware search needed to get the exact length of the substring in the `sourceString` that is matched by `searchString`?
The readme mentioned that exactly length cannot be calculated because of `As we are normalizing strings to be able to cut them, we cannot calculate the match length on the original strings`.
Is it because we normalize the source string that we cannot calculate the length because the expected match length is based on the number of unicode code points?

I'm wondering if it is at all possible to
```
// If no match with same normalization form, early return
if (not source.precomposed match search.precomposed)
    return 0;

// Iterate over each character and add number of unicode code points
foreach (search.char)
   if (source[i] match search.char.precomposed)
       matchLength += search.char.precomposed number of code points
   else if (source[i] match search.char.decomposed)
       matchLength += search.char.decomposed number of code points
```
